data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2337,"item_id":"fc_088631ca57ad9a65016adb1d9f1af48191803049aeb3f25563","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"Let n,m be positive integers; u:R^n×(0,∞)→R^m jointly smooth and q∈R^m have Euclidean norm one. Assume |u(x,r)|=1; for each (x,r) there is a∈R with u_tt−Δ_xu=a u; and on each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), u=q outside a compact C_J uniformly for r∈J. Define e(x,r)=|u_t|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u|² and E(r)=∫_{R^n}e(x,r)dx, Lebesgue measure, Euclidean norms. Prove e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable for each r>0, E is differentiable for each r>0, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"m\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"u\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"jointly smooth map R^n×(0,∞)→R^m\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"q\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"unit vector in R^m\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-10\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:11-13\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:14-16\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D001\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n×(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"e(x,r)=|u_t(x,r)|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u(x,r)|²\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D002\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"E\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"E(r)=Lebesgue integral over R^n of e(x,r)\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"D001\\\"],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D003\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Δ_x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"operator on smooth R^m-valued maps\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"Δ_xu=Σ_{j=1}^n∂²_{x_j}u, componentwise\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]}],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Finite Euclidean inner-product and sum calculations; one-variable fundamental theorem of calculus; compact-box uniform continuity; Fubini for continuous compactly supported functions.\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"real numbers\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"real field, topology, and Lebesgue measure\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R^k\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Euclidean space\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"k-dimensional real Euclidean space with Lebesgue measure and Euclidean inner product\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"4.32.2\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"/Users/syyui/formalization-tools/lean-mathlib-v4.32.2/mathlib\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"problem.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"proof-draft.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"source-context.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"}]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"q\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(·,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"u\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real number\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Let r0 be arbitrary in (0,∞).\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact interval in (0,∞) with r0 in its interior\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose a compact interval about r0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact subset of R^n\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose the compact support set supplied by H003 for J.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"J\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"J\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"B\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"closed box in R^n containing C_J\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose a sufficiently large closed box containing the compact set C_J.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"C_J\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"C_J\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"u_t\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"time derivative of u\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Write u_t for the time derivative of u.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"u_j\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"spatial derivative ∂_{x_j}u\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Write u_j for ∂_{x_j}u.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"u_{tt}\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"second time derivative of u\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Write u_{tt} for the second time derivative of u.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\"]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r0>0 and choose a compact interval J about it. By H003 choose compact C_J. The map equals the constant q on the open complement of C_J, so all first derivatives vanish there; continuity implies they vanish on the boundary as well. Thus e(·,r) is continuous, bounded on C_J and zero off C_J, proving its Lebesgue integrability. Choose a closed box B containing C_J. On B, e and its time derivative are continuous; the time derivative is uniformly continuous on B×J. For h→0 the one-variable fundamental theorem of calculus writes the difference quotient of e as the average of its time derivative between r0 and r0+h. Uniform continuity gives uniform convergence on B, so finite measure of B allows integration of the limit. Hence E'(r0)=∫_B e_t(x,r0)dx. Differentiating the finite sum defining e gives e_t=2u_t·u_tt+2Σ_j u_j·∂_j u_t. For each j, the smooth compactly supported scalar product u_t·u_j has spatial derivative whose integral is zero: integrate first in x_j by the one-dimensional fundamental theorem of calculus, then in the other variables by Fubini, applicable since the derivative is continuous and compactly supported. Thus ∫u_j·∂_j u_t=−∫u_t·∂_j u_j. Summing yields E'(r0)=2∫u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu). Differentiating |u|²=1 once in time gives u·u_t=0. By H002, pointwise u_tt−Δ_xu=a u for some scalar a; hence u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu)=0. The integral is zero. Since r0 was arbitrary the conclusion holds for every positive time.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\",\\\"J\\\",\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"B\\\",\\\"u_t\\\",\\\"u_j\\\",\\\"u_{tt}\\\",\\\"u\\\",\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[]}]}}\"}"}

